-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, and the question rows from the
-- committed bank JSONs under tools/course-banks/marine/advanced.
--
-- What this tier owns: SHORE BASE QUEUES, VARIABILITY AND THE LIMITS. The
-- working-hour clock, the service time and the berth utilisation; M/M/c by
-- Erlang C with the published tables and their printed slip; M/D/c by the
-- Cosmetatos approximation and the berth target; the fleet under weather and
-- demand variability through the seeded canonical Monte Carlo, taught with its
-- seed and draws and never graded; the readings, the boundaries and what the
-- engine does not compute.
--
-- AN APP COURSE. The Suite app is the Marine Logistics Planner; the practicals
-- also run in the course's own shore base and variability calculators. The
-- capstone grades six values of this tier, each identical under every reading
-- the engine states and never a Monte Carlo draw.
-- ============================================================================

